.*---------------------------------------------------------------------
:HELP   NAME='ENVIRONMNT'.Environment
:XH3.Environment
:p.This field shows what environment the program is being run in. It may
show the company name for the production environment or something like Test
for a test environment.
:P.Screen: USRMSTF1 Field: ENVIRONMNT
Type: CHAR(40)
Location: (1,47)
:EHELP.
.*---------------------------------------------------------------------
:HELP   NAME='PGMNME'.Program Name
:XH3.Program Name
:p.This is the name of the program being run. It is helpful to reference
when contacting I/T.
:P.Screen: USRMSTF1 Field: PGMNME
Type: CHAR(10)
Location: (1,122)
:EHELP.
.*---------------------------------------------------------------------
:HELP   NAME='MDE'.Program Mode
:XH3.Program Mode
:p.Many programs can be called in different modes. This field shows what
mode the program is running in. The following are some common modes.
:ul.
:li.View/Inquiry - The information on the screen is display only, it cannot
be updated.
:li.Update/Revise - The data on the screen can be changed.
:li.Add - A new record can be added.
:li.Deactivate - The entry will be deactivated when the Enter key is pressed.
:li.Reinstate/Reactivate - The entry will be reinstated when the Enter key
is pressed.
:eul.
:P.Screen: USRMSTF1 Field: MDE
Type: CHAR(10)
Location: (2,2)
:EHELP.
.*---------------------------------------------------------------------
:HELP   NAME='SCHVAL'.Display Search Value
:XH3.Display Search Value
:P.Help text not entered.
:P.Screen: USRMSTF1 Field: SCHVAL
Type: CHAR(40)
Location: (4,9)
:EHELP.
